---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { companyName, supportEmail, onyx } from '../config/site';

const lastUpdated = 'June 22, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Terms of Use — ${companyName}`}
  description={`Terms of Use for ${companyName} mobile applications, including ${onyx.fullName} and ONYX Black subscriptions.`}
  path="/terms"
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <header>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-text sm:text-4xl">
        Terms of Use
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-custom mt-12 space-y-10 text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Agreement</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          These Terms of Use ("Terms") govern your access to and use of mobile applications
          published by {companyName} ("Pixel Arc Labs," "I," "me," or "my"), including{' '}
          {onyx.fullName} ("ONYX" or the "App"). By downloading, installing, or using the App,
          you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the App.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          These Terms apply in addition to Apple's{' '}
          <a
            href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/"
            class="text-accent transition-colors hover:text-accent-hover focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent rounded-sm"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            target="_blank"
          >
            Licensed Application End User License Agreement
          </a>{' '}
          ("Apple EULA") where applicable. To the extent of any conflict between these Terms
          and the Apple EULA regarding use of the App on Apple devices, the Apple EULA
          controls.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">The App</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          ONYX is a personal bill and money tracker for iPhone. The App helps you record
          bills, accounts, income, and related information. Features may change over time as
          I improve the App.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          ONYX is not a bank, lender, financial advisor, tax preparer, or payment processor.
          Information in the App is for your personal organization only and should not be
          treated as financial, legal, or tax advice.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Accounts and your data</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Some features require an account. You are responsible for maintaining the security
          of your credentials and for activity under your account. You agree to provide
          accurate information and to use the App lawfully.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          You retain ownership of content you enter into the App. You grant me a limited
          license to host, process, and sync that content solely to operate the App and
          provide support. How I handle personal information is described in my{' '}
          <a
            href="/privacy"
            class="text-accent transition-colors hover:text-accent-hover focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent rounded-sm"
          >
            Privacy Policy
          </a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">ONYX Black subscriptions</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          ONYX Black is an optional auto-renewing subscription that unlocks premium
          features such as data export, home screen widgets, unlimited accounts, and bank
          account sync (when available). Free features of ONYX remain available without a
          subscription.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-text">Billing through Apple</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          All purchases and subscriptions are processed by Apple through your Apple ID. I do
          not collect or store your payment card details. Apple's terms and privacy policy
          apply to payment processing.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-text">Plans, pricing, and free trials</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          ONYX Black may be offered as monthly and/or annual subscriptions. Prices are
          displayed in the App before you confirm a purchase and may vary by region. From
          time to time I may offer a free trial or introductory period. If a free trial is
          offered, you will see the trial length and the price that applies after the trial
          before you subscribe.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Unless you cancel at least 24 hours before the end of a trial or current billing
          period, your subscription automatically renews and your Apple ID is charged for
          the next period at the then-current price.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-text">Managing and cancelling</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          You can manage or cancel a subscription at any time in your Apple ID account
          settings:
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          <a
            href="https://apps.apple.com/account/subscriptions"
            class="text-accent transition-colors hover:text-accent-hover focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent rounded-sm"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            target="_blank"
          >
            apps.apple.com/account/subscriptions
          </a>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Deleting the App does not cancel your subscription. Refunds are handled by Apple
          according to Apple's policies; contact Apple Support for billing disputes or refund
          requests.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-text">Restore purchases</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          If you reinstall the App or use a new device, use "Restore purchases" in the App
          to reactivate ONYX Black on the same Apple ID used for the original purchase.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Acceptable use</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">You agree not to:</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
          <li>Use the App for any unlawful purpose or in violation of applicable laws</li>
          <li>Attempt to reverse engineer, decompile, or extract source code from the App</li>
          <li>Interfere with or disrupt the App, servers, or networks connected to the App</li>
          <li>Access the App through unauthorized automated means</li>
          <li>Misrepresent your identity or impersonate another person</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Third-party services</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          The App may integrate with third-party services (for example, cloud sync,
          authentication, analytics, or bank linking through Plaid). Those services are
          governed by their own terms and policies. I am not responsible for third-party
          services outside my reasonable control.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Disclaimers</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          THE APP IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE" WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND,
          WHETHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
          FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. I DO NOT WARRANT THAT THE
          APP WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED, ERROR-FREE, OR COMPLETELY SECURE.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          You use the App at your own risk. You are solely responsible for financial
          decisions you make and for verifying amounts, due dates, and account information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, {companyName.toUpperCase()} AND ITS OWNER
          WILL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR
          PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR ANY LOSS OF PROFITS, DATA, OR GOODWILL, ARISING FROM YOUR
          USE OF THE APP. MY TOTAL LIABILITY FOR ANY CLAIM RELATING TO THE APP WILL NOT
          EXCEED THE GREATER OF (A) THE AMOUNT YOU PAID FOR ONYX BLACK IN THE TWELVE (12)
          MONTHS BEFORE THE CLAIM OR (B) FIFTY U.S. DOLLARS ($50).
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Some jurisdictions do not allow certain limitations, so some of the above may not
          apply to you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Changes</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          I may update these Terms from time to time. When I do, I will revise the "Last
          updated" date above. Material changes may also be communicated in the App or on
          this website. Continued use after changes take effect constitutes acceptance of
          the updated Terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Questions about these Terms? Contact {companyName} at{' '}
          <a
            href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}
            class="text-accent transition-colors hover:text-accent-hover focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent rounded-sm"
          >
            {supportEmail}
          </a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-16">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="text-sm text-text-muted transition-colors hover:text-accent focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent rounded-sm"
      >
        &larr; Back to home
      </a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
